Setup for a potential of a patch disk, see Creasey, Theuns &
Bower, 2013, MNRAS, Volume 429, Issue 3, p.1922-1948

The disc mid-plane is perpendicular to the x-axis, at x = x_disc
(DiscPatchPotential:x_disc in disc-patch.yml). The density is given by
rho(x) = (Sigma/2b) / cosh^2(x/b)
where x is measured from the mid-plane, Sigma is the surface density,
and b the scale height.

The corresponding force is
dphi/dx = 2 pi G Sigma tanh(x/b),
which satisfies d^2phi/dx^2 = 4 pi G rho.
